# Read aloud and left as it is, so that this is a decision and not an
# oversight. `contains` takes a list, a map or a string, and only the string
# branch requires a string needle -- `contains([1], 1)` is fine. The message
# states that rule without its condition: true of this call, not of the
# builtin. The clause was not added because the reader of this message has
# already been told exactly what to change, and docs/spec.md carries the
# condition where someone learning `contains` will meet it.
print(contains("abc", 1))
